<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a null pointer dereference in `glslang::HlslParseContext::wrapupSwitchSubsequence`. The `switchSequence` pointer is null when `switchSequence->size()` is called. This indicates a bug in the glslang library's handling of `switch` statements, likely due to an unexpected or malformed input shader generated by the fuzzer.

A null check should be added before dereferencing `switchSequence` in `/src/glslang/glslang/HLSL/hlslParseHelper.cpp:9370`.

```cpp
// In /src/glslang/glslang/HLSL/hlslParseHelper.cpp:9370
if (switchSequence) { // Add this null check
for (unsigned int s = 0; s < switchSequence->size(); ++s) {
...
}
}
```
</crash-analysis>

